From 27c0a7deff65bd7c6612cf587c3cdf8b56e381af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:19:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Noah-MP: condense the water for negative transpiration
 heat on the canopy

vege_flux can return a negative transpiration heat flux (fctr < 0: vapour
condensing through the stomatal pathway). canwater takes
etran = max(fctr/hvap, 0), so that latent heat warms the canopy but no
water condenses: Noah-MP's water and its latent heat flux disagree.

Count that condensation as dew (or frost, on a frozen canopy) on the
canopy, through the existing qdewc/qfroc pathway. The energy solution is
unchanged; only the water follows it.

Port of the ufs-community/ccpp-physics fix (same code), measured in UFS
(C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, 24 h, all water fixes): fctr < 0 on 13 % of
column-steps; Noah-MP's latent energy exceeded the latent energy of its water
by 0.024 W/m2 per land column, 0.0013 W/m2 with the fix (the canopy
evaporation cap). About 8e-4 mm/day more canopy dew over land; water closure
unchanged.

Measured with the rest of this series in the land component
(datm_cdeps_lnd_gswp3, 24 h, a water meter in noahmpdrv_run): Noah-MP's
water-check residual summed over land points was -1.50 mm (-5.2e-4 of the
precipitation, one-signed) before the series and -2.3e-9 mm (-8e-13) after;
the metered original reproduces the regression baseline.

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
---
 src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 b/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
index 27fd78b..5e385da 100644
--- a/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
+++ b/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
@@ -7318,7 +7318,8 @@ zolmax = xkrefsqr / sqrt(xkzo)   ! maximum z/L
       if (.not.frozen_canopy) then             ! barlage: change to frozen_canopy
         etran = max( fctr/hvap, 0. )
         qevac = max( fcev/hvap, 0. )
-        qdewc = abs( min( fcev/hvap, 0. ) )
+        ! condensation in the transpiration pathway (fctr < 0) is dew on the canopy
+        qdewc = abs( min( fcev/hvap, 0. ) ) + abs( min( fctr/hvap, 0. ) )
         qsubc = 0.
         qfroc = 0.
       else
@@ -7326,7 +7327,7 @@ zolmax = xkrefsqr / sqrt(xkzo)   ! maximum z/L
         qevac = 0.
         qdewc = 0.
         qsubc = max( fcev/hsub, 0. )
-        qfroc = abs( min( fcev/hsub, 0. ) )
+        qfroc = abs( min( fcev/hsub, 0. ) ) + abs( min( fctr/hsub, 0. ) )
       endif
 
 ! canopy water balance. for convenience allow dew to bring canliq above
